  "commit_message": "[mypyc] Import setuptools lazily in mypyc.build on Python 3.12+  (#22084)\n\nImporting mypyc.build used to always import setuptools, distutils and\nmypyc.build_setup, but mypyc_build (type checking and C generation)\nneeds none of them. They are only needed for building extensions, e.g. \nin mypycify. Importing them is slow, which adds significant fixed \noverhead to tools that call mypyc_build directly for many small builds, \nsuch as Bazel integrations.\n\nMove these imports into a helper function, cal",
